"""stage1c_table.py (kit v12): score G016 stage 1c from the driver's results.txt files (RESULT, WINDOW, DROP, PREFETCH, TRACE lines).
Kit v12 runs the driver twice: no MEM_MAX with arms F N (2 rounds, the no-cap stage) and MEM_MAX=1536M with arms F N
(2 rounds, the capped stage). Give the results.txt files in any order; a file's level is read from its RESULT lines'
mem_max. A W/V diagnosis file is optional and scored only if given (the one with W/V).
Prints a per-run table, per level and arm medians [min-max], a verdict for E1-E10, and the decision lines.
usage: python3 -I stage1c_table.py <stage1c dir>/results.txt [<stage1c dir>/results.txt ...]

Arms: F = 3h (3f's LMDB drop plus the pruning prefetch) with its drop on; N = the same binary with it off (MONERODATO_NO_DROP_FREED=1, .6's path); W = kit v9's
3e with a page-event log, traced; V = 3f with the page-event log, traced.
The heavy part is windows k=2..7 of 1,000 blocks (heights 3,107,401-3,113,400). Its rate is 6,000 blocks over the sum of
those windows' seconds; its reads are the mean of their read_kB_per_block. Windows 6-7 (3,111,401-3,113,400) are where
kit v9's 3e read without a cap.
A missing run, window or file, or an na value, counts as not met, with the reason printed."""
import re, statistics, sys

TOP = 3113400
REF = {TOP: "5a956cc4b1d19d21423fa11292a1c5f2496111e1a7d39562f4d2287284036361"}
CAP = "1536M"           # the capped stage's MEM_MAX
EXPECTED = {CAP: 2, "none": 2}   # F and N runs per arm at each level
